WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.660
Frozen 16 megabyte tables let laptop CPUs run 46 megabyte ternary models at 615 tokens per second. They match float baselines on Lambada and PIQA, peaking at 740 tokens per second. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 208. Researchers swap the full-learned embedding table in a Gemma-shaped 270 million parameter model for a table of 512 bit codes, according to a new archive paper. Those codes come from principal component projection,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.680
and signed binarization of a pre-trained embedding, and the frozen table is then trained

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:41.460
from scratch on 2.05 billion tokens. A learned table still cuts validation loss by 0.20

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.020
Nats, yet the frozen version matches or beats it on Helliswag as well.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.080
Paired with a ternary bitnet B1.58 body, the network sits in 62 megabytes of memory and

00:00:53.080 --> 00:01:00.300
runs 5-6 times faster than the float models 8-bit GGUF in Lama.CPP at roughly 1-7th

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.520
the memory. After training, the frozen table accepts 10,000 new words at a 3% cost, while

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:12.580
the learned table collapses by 43%. All weights, data, and evaluation answers are released.

00:01:13.644 --> 00:01:19.834
Synthetic target languages numbering 96 let GPT-2 small models train from scratch, while

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:25.574
clause word order, noun phrase order, alignment, complement system, and action nominal strategy

00:01:25.574 --> 00:01:28.134
all vary in work posted to archive.

00:01:28.794 --> 00:01:34.374
Targeted minimal pair evaluation across 34 grammatical phenomena shows typological parallels

00:01:34.374 --> 00:01:36.134
in basic clause configurations.

00:01:36.794 --> 00:01:42.034
Clear divergences appear in complement systems and action nominal strategies, and the models

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.894
also acquire combinations rare or unattested in natural languages.

00:01:45.894 --> 00:01:53.057
PurlChat is an 8.47 million-parameter causal decoder-only transformer built for Luganda from

00:01:53.057 --> 00:02:00.937
first principles in Jaxx and Flax NNX, detailed in an archive NLP paper. A bite-level BPE tokenizer

00:02:00.937 --> 00:02:08.637
that's bite-paring coding, with a vocabulary of 8,192 achieves 1.60 tokens per word fertility.

00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:15.597
Two-stage training on 59,501 pre-training sequences and 510 instruction dialogues

00:02:16.257 --> 00:02:22.017
drops validation cross entropy from 9.4695 to 0.1818 NATS.

00:02:22.357 --> 00:02:30.677
The model reaches 0.9792 Rouge L and 0.9405 BU on a held out diagnostic benchmark while

00:02:30.677 --> 00:02:32.977
preserving band 2 noun class concord.

00:02:33.854 --> 00:02:40.114
A language-agnostic pipeline denoises noisy knowledge-based text alignments with a natural language inference

00:02:40.114 --> 00:02:46.994
filter, called NLI, and releases Heary, a 1.5 million-instance silver data set for Hebrew

00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:48.094
relation extraction.

00:02:48.814 --> 00:02:58.814
Gemma 431B reaches 0.915F1, matching GPT 5.4 at 0.921, according to the archive writeup.

00:02:59.354 --> 00:03:05.954
On a fully held out dual annotated test set, the same Gemma checkpoint scores 0.844F1.

00:03:05.954 --> 00:03:12.835
Experiments across US, Dutch, and Chinese contexts find that large language models overpredict

00:03:12.835 --> 00:03:15.395
stereotypes, and archive study reports.

00:03:16.055 --> 00:03:18.995
Non-English prompts improve cultural context consideration.

00:03:19.815 --> 00:03:24.935
Additional instruction tuning reduces false positive rates, while training data size moderates

00:03:24.935 --> 00:03:27.215
detection effectiveness non-monotonically.

00:03:28.158 --> 00:03:33.898
Causal latent workspaces add prefix-specific latent slots that each position writes to and

00:03:33.898 --> 00:03:39.318
from before the next shared block, in a four-round shared depth looped transformer described on

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:47.498
archive. At 101.71 million parameters, the model leads on WikiText 103 raw, eWik8, and tiny

00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:55.378
stories. Proplexity improves 0.73 to 1.06% over the strongest non-workspace control across nine

00:03:55.378 --> 00:04:01.773
seeds. An inductive framework combines full and partial colexification networks with short concept

00:04:01.773 --> 00:04:05.993
descriptions to embed previously unseen concepts according to Archive.

00:04:06.453 --> 00:04:11.533
The resulting embeddings correlate with cross-linguistic similarity measures and generalize to

00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:13.273
nodes absent from training data.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:20.290
Real CLI introduces a paired benchmark that measures both task execution and human agent collaboration

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:25.990
quality for command line interface agents or CLI agents in a new Archive paper.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:38.650
Real CLI XX supplies complete specifications, while real CLI collab uses a scripted user delivering progressive corrections, scoring 22 sub-dimensions across 51 interaction templates.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:46.410
Frontier agents reach at most 49.2% average score, and 37.6% joint collaboration score.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:52.230
Consistent shortfalls show up in steerability, trust calibration, and safety boundary management.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:58.783
A single injected passage succeeds in up to 61% of cases across two medical multi-agent

00:04:58.783 --> 00:05:02.543
systems and three benchmarks, researchers show on archive.

00:05:03.023 --> 00:05:05.863
Collaboration does not reliably protect against attack.

00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:11.243
A training-free defense that separates patient findings from clinical judgments and verifies

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:18.043
each judgment against findings alone lowers attack success on MedQA to 4-7% while preserving

00:05:18.043 --> 00:05:19.583
accuracy on clean cases.

00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:27.622
Pro per Mem pairs egocentric video with year-long distractor-rich memories, averaging 618,000 tokens,

00:05:28.162 --> 00:05:31.002
and human verified trigger windows, according to Archive.

00:05:31.442 --> 00:05:37.962
Pro per agent surfaces relevant memory via a graph store and gates it to avoid unnecessary interruptions.

00:05:38.422 --> 00:05:48.542
Strict accuracy rises from below 10% to 37.5% on QN 3.827b and 38% on GPT 5.3 chat,

00:05:48.542 --> 00:05:54.302
without additional training. Reinforcement learning post-training reaches 42.4%.

00:05:55.212 --> 00:05:59.132
Execution guided tool use over large libraries isolates candidate

00:05:59.132 --> 00:06:04.232
investigations in separate branches, executes each, then adopts only useful

00:06:04.232 --> 00:06:10.232
results into the main trajectory, work on archive names Briai. On MCP Atlas, with a

00:06:10.232 --> 00:06:18.312
shared pool of 1,897 tools, it achieves an average claim score of 89.77, a 14.37

00:06:18.312 --> 00:06:20.412
7-point gain over MCP0.

00:06:20.672 --> 00:06:25.552
The method remains on the Pareto Frontier for performance versus input token cost.

00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:32.658
Public data sets totaling 77 sources feed a 141 million parameter encoder, trained on

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:39.058
1.12 million examples relabeled under a consistent 12-category schema for personally identifiable

00:06:39.058 --> 00:06:42.758
information, or PII, and archive paper shows.

00:06:42.758 --> 00:06:53.438
It achieves the highest recall against larger baselines in 11 of 14 comparisons on AI4 privacy and Nemotron PII at a low false positive operating point.

00:06:53.838 --> 00:06:59.998
Throughput is 2 to 10 times higher with 94 to 97% less peak GPU memory than the baselines.

00:07:00.995 --> 00:07:11.135
Layerwise unlearning that touches only one selected transformer layer uses confidence weighted forgetting and retain regularization in a method called KOLU, posted to archive.

00:07:11.135 --> 00:07:18.095
On Tofu, it improves both forgetting and retention over NPO, SAT-imp, and GA-based foam UL

00:07:18.095 --> 00:07:19.235
in all six settings.

00:07:19.775 --> 00:07:24.535
On Mews, it records the highest retained no-mem and privilege, closest to zero, among

00:07:24.535 --> 00:07:31.795
compared methods, while using 77.4 to 79.5% less GPU memory than full model unlearning.

00:07:32.748 --> 00:07:37.928
Token Economizer is an external controller that learns which micro-skills to inject, which

00:07:37.928 --> 00:07:42.108
Each irrelevant tools to prune and went to break unproductive loops across sequences

00:07:42.108 --> 00:07:45.228
of realistic coding tasks, according to Archive.

00:07:45.628 --> 00:07:52.928
It reduces average token cost 18.4% to 30.9% for Clawed Code, Codex, and GitHub Copilot

00:07:52.928 --> 00:07:56.988
CLI paired with Frontier models while preserving task success.

00:07:57.708 --> 00:08:00.748
Savings generalized to web development and security auditing.

00:08:01.802 --> 00:08:06.702
Joint embedding guided pruning trains a public reference model on PII free views of the

00:08:06.702 --> 00:08:12.362
same records and uses cross-model representation probes, plus integrated gradients to identify

00:08:12.362 --> 00:08:16.582
and prune 1.6% of neurons, and archive paper reports.

00:08:17.402 --> 00:08:23.922
PII inference accuracy drops up to 7.4 times and extraction recall up to 13.9 times.

00:08:24.542 --> 00:08:30.162
Unseen text perplexity stays within 16% of the unprune model for most large language models.

00:08:31.051 --> 00:08:35.151
Pull the release ternary checkpoint with the frozen embedding table and time it against

00:08:35.151 --> 00:08:38.691
your current 8-bit GGUF setup on the same laptop CPU.

00:08:39.391 --> 00:08:44.831
Score your own CLI agent in both real CLI modes, so you can separate RAW task completion

00:08:44.831 --> 00:08:46.731
from how it handles a correcting user.

00:08:47.391 --> 00:08:52.711
If a fine-tuned domain model is leaking PII, run the J-PAPRUN recipe on it rather than

00:08:52.711 --> 00:08:53.851
starting a full retrain.

00:08:54.511 --> 00:08:59.451
On a library of a few hundred functions, try Bria's pattern of inspecting tools and separate

00:08:59.451 --> 00:09:02.871
execution branches before adopting results into the main trajectory.

00:09:02.871 --> 00:09:09.307
Low resource NLP groups are expected to release further byte-level BPE tokenizers tuned

00:09:09.307 --> 00:09:10.787
for agglutinative languages.

00:09:11.727 --> 00:09:16.507
Expanded benchmarks that jointly score execution and collaboration quality are likely to appear

00:09:16.507 --> 00:09:19.047
for additional agent domains beyond CLI.

00:09:19.887 --> 00:09:24.487
Lair-wise, unlearning methods that operate on single-selected layers will probably be tested

00:09:24.487 --> 00:09:27.087
on larger open-weight families in the coming weeks.

00:09:28.128 --> 00:09:32.728
One extra-learned parameter per head is the cost when we pop the hood on first passage

00:09:32.728 --> 00:09:38.428
attention. The mechanism replaces monotonic accumulation of decay along the key query path

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:44.968
with a path extreme operation. That operation lowers a key's logit by the deepest dip of a learned

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:50.368
scalar field below that key's level. When the field and the levels follow a shared learned walk,

00:09:50.888 --> 00:09:56.428
the mechanism naturally forms a stack. A constant dimension head can then realize any subset of

00:09:56.428 --> 00:10:02.628
keys left alive by subsequent dips. In synthetic experiments, a single layer FPA head converges

00:10:02.628 --> 00:10:08.108
to the target-alive key sets on every seed. Comparable softmax and forgetting transformer

00:10:08.108 --> 00:10:13.608
baselines fail on all seeds. At 110 million parameters, the model matches forgetting

00:10:13.608 --> 00:10:19.348
transformer perplexity. It still achieves perfect pasky retrieval at 8 times the training length,

00:10:19.528 --> 00:10:25.508
even when its key value cache is compressed to roughly 25%. The added scalar field introduces

00:10:25.508 --> 00:10:30.448
is that one extra learned parameter per head and a small constant time max tracking operation

00:10:30.448 --> 00:10:36.008
per step. Use FPA when long context retrieval stability matters more than the marginal

00:10:36.008 --> 00:10:41.148
training cost of the extra field. The main gotcha is that the learned walk must be shared

00:10:41.148 --> 00:10:46.268
between field and levels, otherwise the stack property disappears and performance falls back

00:10:46.268 --> 00:10:52.784
to soft max levels. Before we go, memory gated proactive agents are lined up for extra reinforcement

00:10:52.784 --> 00:10:56.304
learning stages aimed at cutting early or repeated interruptions.

